          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Co-Founder of Magnum Photos</strong><br>\nCapa was a co-founder of Magnum Photos, an international cooperative photography agency. He envisioned Magnum as a support system for photographers who wished to work outside the constraints of mainstream commercial and media interests.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Post-War Coverage and Legacy</strong><br>\nAfter the war, Capa continued to photograph conflicts, including the Arab-Israeli War in 1948 and the First Indochina War. His commitment to bearing witness to war and its effects on the human spirit defined his career.</p>\n\n<p><strong>\"Slightly Out of Focus\" and Personal Writing</strong><br>\nCapa authored \"Slightly Out of Focus,\" a memoir recounting his wartime experiences with a blend of humor and gravity. This personal account adds to our understanding of Capa's work and his perspective on the chaos of war.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
